# Erosion spline replacement

Replace the old three PCG graphs, their wrappers and all 36 include/exclude box
actors and six box Blueprint assets. Preserve architecture, lighting, asynchronous
environment selection, local Level Instance references and editor preview.

Each erosion owns an independent spline-region Blueprint and native PCG graph.
Regions attach to their own ErosionLayout. RegionMode switches Include/Exclude;
an exclusion always wins. Width, edge falloff and projection depth shape each
region. Include regions now also own MaxCount, Density, PackingGap and
PackingBoundsScale, with ActualCount showing the final result. Spline points
remain editable with the ordinary viewport handles.
Open ribbons are the first supported authoring form, including vertical walls.

Generation uses randomized surface candidates, spline density, large/medium/small
stages per Include, cross-spline overlap pruning and small-point gap filling.
Mesh/weight arrays, count,
size proportions/ranges, sampling spacing, packing clearance, rotation, attachment
depth, density and seed remain editable. Internal trace/noise/pruning switches
are fixed. All names/categories are English and tooltips Korean. Runtime is
Blueprint and native PCG only; Python is authoring/verification only.

Verification must cover all three erosions in source RXPart, two transformed
Level Instances, PIE selected-only loading and matching preview/runtime results.
Required deltas: spline shape/width, Include/Exclude toggle, independent erosion
edits, mesh overrides/weights, count, size, spacing and packing. Test exclusion
precedence, wall-back rejection, non-grid placement, finite candidate budget and
cleanup of old actors/assets/references. Capture actual generated results.
Promote only after dependency audit, Blueprint compile and full regression gate.

Per-spline controls are implemented by three native packing workers and one
shared native stats worker. Exclusions apply before local packing. Candidate
slots are reserved evenly per Include, including disabled Includes, and rounded
down to stay within the common budget without reallocating other regions.
BoundsScale adjusts pruning bounds about their centre and does not rescale meshes;
values below 1 permit actual mesh penetration. MaxCount is an upper limit.
RebuildPreview on a region forwards to its attached Layout's dispatcher. The
editor-only preview registers only on its own Layout and unbinds the prior Layout
before rebinding. Layout has no Preview class/PCG graph hard dependency. Counts
update after global pruning; excludes and inactive
erosions reset to zero. Preview remains editor-only but uses an Actor parent for
calls from ordinary BPs. Nine migrated Layout variables are removed with an exact
allowlist after live PCG and BP consumer audits and independent review.
